    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="30">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 30</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>XXV. Gif hit sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.12"/> syxhynde mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.7"/>, ælc mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.star2"/> to hloðbote LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.17"/> scill., ⁊ se slaga wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.13"/> ⁊ fulwite.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.18"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>XXIIII. Gif hit sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.4"/> syxhynde mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.3"/>, ælc mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.3"/> to hloðbote LX scll', ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.3"/> se slaga wer ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.3"/> fulwite.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>Be sixhyndu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> m<hi rend="italic">en</hi>. Gyf hit sy syxhynde man, ælc to hloðbote feowertig [scill'<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.2"/>], ⁊ se slaga were ⁊ fulwite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="65" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.7-2"/> sit homo sixhindus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.8"/>, unusquisque reddat pro hloþbota<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.4-2"/> LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_30.lnote.oe.9"/> sol., et percussor weram cum plena wita.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="76" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be sixhyndum men.] Gif hit sie syxhynde mon, ælc mon [geselle]<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Af_30.attnote.fn.4"/> to hloðbote LX<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Af_30.attnote.fn.5"/> scill., ⁊ se slaga wer<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Af_30.attnote.fn.6"/> ⁊ fulwite<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Af_30.attnote.fn.7"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="30.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="322" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XXV} Gif hit sie syxhynde mon, ælc mon to hloðbote LX scill, ⁊ se slaga wer ⁊ fulwite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="65" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn es ein 600 [Schilling-]Mann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_30.lnote.de.1"/> ist, [zahle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_30.lnote.de.2"/>] jeder Begleiter als Bandenbusse 60<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_30.lnote.de.3"/> Schill., und der Todtschläger [selbst] Wergeld und Vollstrafe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_30.lnote.de.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If it is a 600[-shilling] man, [let] each companion [pay] 60 shillings as band-compensation, and the slayer [himself] the wergeld and the full fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="77" ed="#attenborough"/>If the slain man's wergeld is 600 shillings, each man shall pay 60 shillings for belonging to such a band; and the homicide [shall pay] the wergeld and the full fine<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_30.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="413" ed="#whitelock"/>If it is a man of a six-hundred wergild, each man [is to pay] 60 shillings as compensation for being in that band, and the slayer the wergild and full fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="323" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If it is a 600-[wergild] man, let each man give 60 shillings as compensation for taking part in the band, and the slayer <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> and full fine.</ab>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">Whitelock numbers this chapter 30 and gives Liebermann’s number, 30, in brackets.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">man Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mon geselle to hloðbót <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> ælc to hloþebót gesylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mon geselle to hloðbót So; ælc to hloþebót gesylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">syxtig</hi> <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">syxtig</hi> So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">were <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">were So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wite <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wite So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> fullw.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to fullw.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Si — hloþbota <hi rend="italic">überspringt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Si — hloþbota skipped by Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-hyn. <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> -hun. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-hyn. T; -hun. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lo. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lo. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XL <hi rend="italic">Hn</hi> 87, 4 (<hi rend="italic">wie B</hi>)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XL Hn 87, 4 (as B)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">später übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above later</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu Inst. <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl: radcniht</hi> (auch zu Af 39, 2), worüber auch J Earle im <hi rend="italic">Archaeol. Journal</hi> 19, 55, Hale <hi rend="italic">Domesday of St. Paul’s</hi> p. <hi rend="smallcaps">xxix</hi>, Pol Mai I 528 handeln. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Sechshunderter 1. 3. 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On Inst. <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl: radcniht</hi> (also on Af 39, 2), which is also discussed by J Earle in the <hi rend="italic">Archaeol. Journal</hi> 19, 55, Hale <hi rend="italic">Domesday of St. Paul’s</hi> p. <hi rend="smallcaps">xxix</hi>, and Pol Mai I 528. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Sechshunderter 1. 3. 6</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aus So Ld, unnötige Ergänzung</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from So Ld, an unnecessary supplement</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘40’ B wohl Lesefehler, den unabhängig auch Hn 87, 4 zeigt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘40’ B, probably a misreading, which Hn 87, 4 also shows independently</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_30.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Strafe’ (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 1eB, wo aber gegen S. 668 Z. 2—4 fraglich, ob hiermit 120 Schill. gemeint) als synonym Inst.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘punishment’ (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 1eB, where, however, contrary to p. 668 ll. 2—4, it is questionable whether 120 shill. is meant by this) as a synonym, Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_30.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>geselle</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">So. <hi rend="italic">gesylle</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_30.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>lx</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">feowertig</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_30.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>wer</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">were</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_30.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>fulwite</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">fullwite</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_30.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">196</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">It is not clear whether the full fine is 60 or 120 shillings (see Liebermann’s note <hi rend="italic">ad loc.</hi>).</seg></note>
      </div>
